Description: Q6A camera driver fixes (settle, lane_assign, SOF/EOF, CSIPHY handle, combo_mode, CSID clk floor)
 Radxa Q6A adaptations for camera-driver v1.0.5, taken verbatim from the Yocto
 recipe meta-qcom/recipes-multimedia/camx/camx-dlkm/camx-dlkm-q6a-settle-sof.patch
 (md5 3a7aadda5e8a2875ed41dae68a98a790).
 .
 NOT applied by default - see debian/patches/series.  Measured 2026-09-30 on Q6A
 with IMX577: with this patch applied the preview delivers zero frames at a CSID
 floor of either 400 MHz or 600 MHz (ISP stalls in Substate[BUBBLE], CamX reports
 ParseHangRegDump / errorCode 257), while the unpatched driver runs 1920x1080@30
 NV12 at 29.78 fps with dropped:0 and FIFO_OVERFLOW:0.  Details in
 docs/camx-service-packaging.md section 10.6.
Author: Chongbiao Chen <chenchongbiao@radxa.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-30

From: Chongbiao Chen <chenchongbiao@radxa.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camx-dlkm: Q6A fixes from camx-dlkm-q6a-fixes.patch + CSID 600MHz

Includes previously working Q6A patch (settle, lane_assign, SOF/EOF,
keep CSIPHY handle, combo_mode) plus CSID clk floor 600MHz.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Chongbiao Chen <chenchongbiao@radxa.com>

diff --git a/src/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/isp_hw_mgr/isp_hw/ife_csid_hw/cam_ife_csid_core.c b/src/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/isp_hw_mgr/isp_hw/ife_csid_hw/cam_ife_csid_core.c
